 ## Overview
-This method renders 3D Gaussian splats by submitting instanced geometry (quads) to the standard hardware vertex/fragment pipeline, avoiding the memory overhead of tile-based rasterization [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of efficiently projecting 3D ellipses onto the screen by dynamically sizing quads based on opacity cutoffs and evaluating the Gaussian decay function in the fragment shader [S1, unofficial]. It differs from [Volumetric Spot Noise Rendering](2360-volumetric-spot-noise-rendering.md) by using explicit deterministic paths and geometry instancing for depth/opacity accumulation rather than stochastic noise patterns [S1, S2, unofficial].
+This method renders sorted 2D Gaussians by submitting instanced quads to the standard hardware vertex/fragment pipeline, avoiding the memory overhead of tile-based rasterization [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of efficiently projecting these Gaussians onto the screen by dynamically sizing quads based on opacity cutoffs and evaluating the Gaussian decay function in the fragment shader [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from [Volumetric Spot Noise Rendering](2360-volumetric-spot-noise-rendering.md) by relying on deterministic instanced geometry and standard blending rather than stochastic noise functions and hybrid OIT pipelines [S1, S2, unofficial].
 
